# SRG-APP-000865-AU-000360  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must for password-based authentication, employ
# automated tools to assist the user in selecting strong password
# authenticators.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000865-AU-000360
group:           V-263580
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004065
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None that is configurable: Splunk rejects a password that fails the
                 [splunk_auth] composition rules and reports which rule it failed, which is
                 the only automated assistance the product gives, and it is a consequence
                 of those settings rather than a feature with a setting of its own. Splunk
                 Enterprise 10.4.2 offers no password generator, strength meter, or
                 passphrase suggestion to turn on.

external:        An automated tool that helps a user select a strong authenticator (an
                 approved password manager or generator) - carried by the organization's
                 endpoint tooling.
external:        Where authType is LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO, any password-selection
                 assistance is presented by the directory service or identity provider.

manual_reason:   No conf key enables or configures an automated tool to assist a user in
                 selecting a strong password, so no observed configuration value can decide
                 this requirement; the complexity settings that produce the product's
                 rejection messages are already assessed under SRG-APP-000870.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:441-500 ([splunk_auth]
                 complexity settings; the stanza contains no generator, strength, or
                 suggestion setting)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 has no
                 password generator or strength tool to configure, and its only automated
                 assistance is the rejection message produced by the [splunk_auth]
                 composition settings assessed elsewhere, so this requirement is carried by
                 the organization's endpoint tooling and the identity provider; this
                 determination is from the perspective of the application layer alone.
